  "rationale": "Metoprolol: Bradycardia — beta blockade slows heart rate and AV nodal conduction. Warfarin: Bleeding — anticoagulation reduces clotting capacity; monitor INR and bleeding. Furosemide: Hypokalemia — loop diuresis increases urinary potassium losses. Spironolactone: Hyperkalemia — potassium-sparing aldosterone blockade reduces potassium excretion. Lisinopril: Hyperkalemia — ACE inhibition can reduce aldosterone-mediated potassium excretion."
